<title>MEXICO: ICA, Bufete may link up to bid on Pemex projects.</title>
<headline>ICA, Bufete may link up to bid on Pemex projects.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican construction giants ICA and Bufete Industrial have entered into talks about forming a consortium in order to bid on projects related to the Pemex oil refinery expansion at Cadereyta, an ICA spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;There are talks with Bufete to form a competitive national team, which no doubt would be very competitive with international bidders,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>He said an announcement could be made next month.</p>
<p>The Mexican government has said it will take bids for a $1.2 billion expansion at the Cadereyta refinery in northern Nuevo Leon state. Pemex is the state-owned oil monopoly.</p>
<p>-- Daniel Perez, Monterrey bureau, (528) 345-7677</p>
